    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0152" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1832: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-02T16:00:00+01:00">September 2, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 2—9:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1378. Winterton has requested the Foreign Office to ascertain the views of the
                    United States Government as to the future of the Intergovernmental Committee.
                        Lothian<anchor n="74" xml:id="d118-f1"/> will doubtless raise the question
                    in due course. Winterton expects to resign in any event. Emerson has offered his
                    services to the British Government and if they are accepted he will presumably
                    resign from both his refugee offices.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d118-f1" n="74" xml:id="d118-f1-content">
                <p>The Marquess of Lothian, British Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
